# Raw captures are NOT committed by default.
#
# capture-host.sh masks configuration values, but the free-form artefacts
# (nginx -T, crontabs) are filtered heuristically, not provably. Committing a
# capture must therefore stay a deliberate, reviewed act rather than a side
# effect of `git add -A`.
#
# To commit one after reviewing it:
#     git add -f capture/captures/<host>-<timestamp>
#
# Do not relax this rule by ignoring a narrower path or adding a negation.
captures/
